--- STEP 1: CREATE PROJECT IN VISUAL STUDIO ---
1. Open Visual Studio.
2. Click "Create a new project".
3. In the search box at the top, type: ASP.NET Web Application
4. Select the template named:
   "ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework)" (make sure it has the C# tag).
5. Click "Next".
6. Project name: Demorotator
7. Choose your desired location folder.
8. Click "Create".
9. In the next dialog, select the "Empty" template, check "Web Forms" if visible, and click "Create".

--- STEP 2: CREATE IMAGES FOLDER AND ADD BANNER IMAGES ---
1. In Solution Explorer on the right, right-click the project name "Demorotator".
2. Hover over "Add" -> click "New Folder".
3. Name the folder: Images
4. Copy any two sample picture files into this folder and rename them to:
   - ad1.jpg
   - ad2.jpg

--- STEP 3: CREATE THE ADVERTISEMENT XML FILE (add.xml) ---
1. Right-click the project name "Demorotator" in Solution Explorer.
2. Hover over "Add" -> click "New Item...".
3. Under Visual C# on the left panel, click "Data" (or "General" / "Web").
4. Select "XML File".
5. Set the Name at the bottom to:
   add.xml
6. Click "Add".
7. Delete all default text and paste the complete code from FILE 1 below.
8. Save (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 4: CREATE THE WEB FORM (addrotator.aspx) ---
1. Right-click the project name "Demorotator" in Solution Explorer.
2. Hover over "Add" -> click "New Item...".
3. Under Visual C#, select "Web".
4. From the center list, choose "Web Form" (Do NOT pick "Web Form with Master Page").
5. Name it:
   addrotator.aspx
6. Click "Add".
7. Open "addrotator.aspx", delete all text, and paste the code from FILE 2 below.
8. Save (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 5: RUN AND TEST THE ADROTATOR ---
1. In Solution Explorer, right-click "addrotator.aspx".
2. Click "Set As Start Page".
3. Press F5 (or Ctrl + F5) or click the green Play button ("IIS Express") at the top.
4. The web browser will load with one of the ads displayed.
5. Refresh the page (F5 in browser) multiple times:
   - Notice that the advertisement image switches randomly between ad1.jpg and ad2.jpg based on the impressions count.
   - Clicking the ad banner will redirect you to Google or Microsoft.

